WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.440
Hi. Welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.580
Today we're going to do a review of the whole course.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.520
It's good for me. I would like to do a review myself.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.680
This format of doing separate episodes

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.520
and then doing them at separate times

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.880
you kind of lose the flow of the whole teaching.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:30.559
I thought it would be nice today if we went back

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.560
from the beginning and we went through the flow

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.280
of the whole lam rim teaching that we had. 

00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:42.799
I'm going to do that flow based on the IDIMs, on the idea images,

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.540
that we use to teach the ACI teachers.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.220
The ACI teachers

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.800
are expected to be able to look at one of these pictures

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.480
and identify the idea behind it.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.120
I think, Tim how may we said there's going to be?  A thousand or something?

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.800
How many?

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.639
500, something like that. So it's kind of easy to take an exam, 

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.493
to examine someone just based on the pictures.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.160
So we just throw these pictures at you.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.800
So I challenge you during this review

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
when we put up a picture

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.000
i'll give you a second and see if you 

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.533
can remember what the picture was about?

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:28.000
Okay, and this is a good review

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:32.479
of the entire course that we're doing. All right, here we go...

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.560
First picture Mr. Sejii

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.000
This picture is supposed to remind you

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.420
that we are in the middle of the practices

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.360
 for people of medium capacity

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.440
and what they're trying to get to is nirvana.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.800
They're trying to get out of the wheel of life, out of all suffering for themselves personally.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.560
This is where Buddha taught the three trainings

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.120
that will help you to reach personal your nirvana.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.420
The third training is understanding emptiness, understanding the pen.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.880
The second training is meditation.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.200
On a deep level these two can only be done in a quiet place,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.880
during certain times of the day, when you're really focusing on your meditation mat.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.740
On a deep level,  these two have to be done 

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.865
on special periods of the day.

00:02:34.865 --> 00:02:39.540
But this one, the foundation for those two, which is being nice to other people.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.280
You can call it morality.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.840
You could call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.800
but in the end It's being nice to other people. 

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.840
That's the foundation,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.640
which is always available to us all day long.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.900
This is one of the three extraordinary trainings of buddhism,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.659
meant to help us to reach nirvana.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.049
And it's available to us all day long.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.360
So in this picture,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.360
you can see Seiji helping Geshe Michael to figure out his computer.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.640
Which is one of the nicest things that young people can do for older people.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.959
Next picture; see if you can remember what this picture was?

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.040
Did you guess?

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:34.080
This lady is doing her taxes. What does that make her in this lam rim system?

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.320
it makes her...

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.360
a dharma master. When I say dharma master, or tantric master, 

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:44.544
I know the picture you have in your mind.

00:03:44.544 --> 00:03:48.140
It's a some big lama up on a throne and they have a big yellow hat.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:57.760
Maybe they are ringing a bell and a little drum and they are .....

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.751
And you think; 'oh, that's a dharma master. that's a real dharma master'.

00:04:00.751 --> 00:04:02.900
Or you're thinking of that old picture of Nagarjuna,

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.739
and he's he's all kind of mystical.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.959
In the lam rim, what we learned

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.920
was this woman

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:17.439
she has a couple kids, she's married

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:22.078
and she's a dharma master. She is a real dharma master.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:27.459
Pabongka Rinpoche said, don't think that a dharma master has to be sitting up on a throne

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.660
reciting some tantric ritual.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.960
This lady is doing what?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.760
She's paying her taxes.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.840
To be honest on your taxes is like really difficult in my country.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.320
It might take you weeks to do your taxes and

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.880
to really do them carefully,

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.040
to do them completely honestly,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.759
to pay every single penny you're supposed to pay.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.400
This makes her...

00:04:56.479 --> 00:05:00.639
She has the first of the extraordinary trainings of a good person;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.880
kind to other people.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.400
That makes her a real dharma master.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.920
Forget those pictures you have of lamas with big hats on, 

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.700
and ringing bells. Okay, that's easy.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.420
Anybody can do that.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.720
To be nice to people is difficult

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.079
and to keep your morality, to keep your ethics

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.065
Is also difficult.

00:05:22.065 --> 00:05:24.700
Next one;

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.080
I will give you a moment. Do you remember what this is about?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.240
The quotation in the lam rim was TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.560
A person who is really keeping their vows,

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.720
really keeping their buddhist guidelines, especially the 10 guidelines,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.620
they shine, they actually shine.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:58.656
A person who is making a healthy, modest, low-key effort to keep their commitments,

00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:01.360
to keep the ten good karmas and

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.000
be nice to other people,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.519
they have some kind of a peaceful look on their face,

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.160
they are shining.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.260
When they walk into a room, you know it.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.360
Everyone starts feeling better, like Tim and Seiji.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.860
That's a light of the world. 

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.240
Buddha said, those people are the light of the world. 

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.380
There's a christian expression;

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:32.400
don't put a candle under a basket, let the world see your happy face.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.960
And that's a true guiding light for the whole world. 

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.440
Next picture IDIM#4 

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:57.600
This is a cliff that I went on with my partner Veronica for her birthday, during this lam rim. 

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:06.940
They were talking about the sun setting, which in Tibetan the word is NUB PA.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.580
It's also the word for west because the sun sets in the west;

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.500
NUB PA means

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.080
the sun setting and this is a very sad verb.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.820
This is a very sad idea in the dharma,

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:27.980
The most famous place comes at the end of the Abhidharmakosha; The Treasure House of Higher Wisdom.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.760
The Treasure House of Higher Knowledge by Master Vasabhandu, and he says;

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:39.060
"the sun of the dharma, the light of the dharma, will set in this world."

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.440
We will lose the light of the dharma in this world. This world will go into darkness.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.520
After a certain amount of time,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.560
The teachings of the Buddha will disappear in this world. 

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.060
First they disappear in the minds of people but they're still in libraries.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:59.600
Those books are still in libraries. Probably libraries that John Brady hasn't found yet.

00:08:00.319 --> 00:08:04.239
And then later, they will disappear from the libraries also and then they'll be gone.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.840
I put the picture here because Pabongka Rinpoche made a special point, he said;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:19.520
'if you can't keep your commitments, if you can't keep nice behavior towards other people,

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.640
then we can say the dharma has left this world.'

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.319
The light of the dharma has left this world inside of you.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.780
The sun has set inside your own chest,

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:34.460
which would be a very sad thing if we don't keep our vows.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.560
Next picture.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.200
We called this retreat Love in the Time of the Virus.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:55.440
The point is that during a very difficult time in the world,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.600
if you keep your commitments,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.860
if you are nice to other people

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.320
when things are frightening and scary and the virus is spreading.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.160
We don't know where, we don't know how, and

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.880
we don't know how many people will die.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:16.660
If during those difficult times you do something nice to other people,

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.160
 it's much, much more powerful.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.420
He mentioned, if you remember, a 5-star Buddha paradise,

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.759
which is like a perfect place.

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.839
It's easy to be a good person, everybody there is a good person.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.236
That's no big achievement.                                           That's not a big deal,

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.220
and the seed is not that powerful

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.580
to be nice in a group of nice people.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.880
To be nice when people are attacking you, when people are afraid.

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:47.518
When people are not being nice to each other and to be the one person

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.060
who stands up and shares things in a difficult time -

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.340
then that's an extremely pure person.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:01.500
That's a great karma. That's an incredible karma, much more powerful.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.840
I think this virus is a very good time, and

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.120
it's a very good chance for all of us to show

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.380
- are we really buddhists?  Are we are we really practicing the bodhisattva path?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.560
Can we help others even when things are very hard.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.500
Next picture.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:31.460
This one is hard to remember, i have trouble remembering it.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:36.280
I'm going to give you a second to try to think of what this picture is.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.840
Pabongka Rinpoche was quoting some books

00:10:44.959 --> 00:10:46.959
with a very, very common ending to different books.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:57.760
He quoted a famous one, which is BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.720
may the teachings of the victorious one

00:11:03.519 --> 00:11:05.519
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkapa

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:08.079
spread in this world.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.720
You're thinking, we got to get on the internet. 

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.000
We have to translate this lamrim into many languages.

00:11:17.279 --> 00:11:21.679
We have to try to spread the good word to as many people as we can.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:31.200
That's the end of the prayer and we're supposed to walk out of this lamrim class or video

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.860
and we're supposed to share the dharma with other people.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.280
We're supposed to spread the dharma in the world.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:44.260
In this part of the lamrim, Pabongka Rinpoche said;

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.660
the place you're supposed to spread the dharma is here, inside your own heart.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:56.160
Don't think that spreading the dharma means, trying to translate the videos

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:00.800
into more languages or something like that. That's a very important spreading of the dharma.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.240
But he says, if you spread it in your own heart,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:09.920
then of course it will spread outside of you because the world is coming from your heart,

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.519
from your heart chakra actually.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.860
Next picture #7

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.300
Try to remember what this picture was about. I'll give you a second.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.680
This is a favorite topic of mine;

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:42.000
having a personal relationship with another person, like these two people have.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.866
In my opinion and in tantra, it's one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:51.860
It's one of the greatest things that can happen to you.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.520
 Anybody can tell you the reason the whole world is looking for a partner,

00:12:58.399 --> 00:13:00.082
is that it makes people happy.

00:13:00.082 --> 00:13:03.279
It's one of the greatest happinesses when it's going well.

00:13:04.399 --> 00:13:07.518
It's one of the greatest happinesses you can have but

00:13:08.399 --> 00:13:12.799
you know and I know when it's not going well

00:13:13.519 --> 00:13:16.159
it's one of the greatest miseries in life.

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:19.839
Why is that relevant to this course right here?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.120
If your morality is good

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.360
it's the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:37.040
And if you break your morality, it's the same thing that is going to make you miserable. 

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.320
It's like having a nice woman or man, who is your partner, 

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.620
the same person who makes you totally happy,

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.860
 can also make you totally miserable.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:52.400
So in this case, vinaya, your personal practice of kindness,

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:56.240
good behavior, is being compared to a partner 

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.540
who can either make you be the best thing in your life

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.320
or the worst thing in your life - same person.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:10.120
Next IDIM #8

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.840
This was a complicated one. See if you can remember?

00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:17.519
I'll take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:18.639 --> 00:14:20.639
Thanks Vimala.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:33.560
This actually represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.720
Pulling up a weed represents breaking your commitments.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.260
Why is destroying this plant is breaking your commitment?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:51.560
If you're a gardener you know that you should pull a weed out

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.640
before the seeds are ready.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.380
If you wait until the seeds are ready to drop off,

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.920
and then you pull the plant out

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.560
then you're going to spread about a thousand seeds.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:11.260
For next next month or next year you're going to get thousands of weeds growing back.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.440
So you have to attack those weeds early.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.140
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.360
that Buddha made

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.900
DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I 

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.240
It's better to die

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.479
than to break your vows. Why?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.680
When you break your vows

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.980
you are setting in motion seeds

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.660
which will continue to fall off for many lifetimes.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:49.740
If you die you ruin one body mind complex.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.060
If you die you ruin one very useful temple,

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.360
a physical temple and a mind. You lose one.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.560
But if you break your commitments

00:16:01.279 --> 00:16:04.440
you lose many body mind complexes.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.458
You ruin your body and mind for many lifetimes

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:11.440
And you kind of set seeds into motion

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.280
which are going to ruin many lifetimes. 

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:20.420
Buddha was saying; it's better to die than to break your vows and 

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:27.460
he was not being metaphorical. He was speaking very literally

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.280
when he said that. Better to die than to break your commitments.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.360
There's a joke in the lamrim.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:44.320
We take a vow never to give up bodhichitta even at the cost of our lives. 

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.480
There's a famous statement, all through our whole life we are waiting

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.720
to get put in a prison

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.880
by some evil people.

00:16:57.199 --> 00:17:02.479
They come up with a knife and they say' 'give up your bodhisattva vows or die today'.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.799
Then we're gonna say;

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:06.480
'I choose to die'.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.199
And they kill us. 

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.280
I think all of us are waiting for this ever since we took that vow.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.300
We're all waiting for these guys to show up with knives and  threaten us.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.960
 But actually we're the guys with the knives. We threaten our bodhisattva vows every day.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:31.840
We have to make this decision every day when we decide whether or not to keep our vows carefully.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.860
It's hard to find those guys who put you in jail, and say; 

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.440
I'm going to kill you if you don't give up your  bodhisattva vows.

