See if you can remember. I'm going to give you a minute to try to remember.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.840
This was a reference....

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.039
we have Mixed Nuts translation team

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.559
and we were translating an old vinaya text;

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.440
monk's vows, nun's vows.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:25.140
They were talking about the vow, the tradition that we shouldn't ...

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:29.820
...when you become a monk or a nun they give you your robes,

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.840
they give you a small buddhist statue,

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.960
and they give you a strainer.

00:18:35.919 --> 00:18:39.279
And in ancient India you were supposed to carry this strainer around with you.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.360
When you drink water from a stream

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.439
you're supposed to strain the water first to make sure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.680
We mentioned a famous tradition in the vinaya, 

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.200
 if a couple of monks go down to the water,

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.380
down to the stream to get some water,

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:07.340
then they should choose the nicest monk to check the water.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:15.040
Don't choose the guy who doesn't care about bugs. Try to find a guy who loves bugs

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.280
and have them check the water because they will be more careful.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.000
What's the point?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.440
We talked about kind of ecology vows,

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:31.540
where monks and nuns are not supposed to even pull green leaves off 

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:37.560
