You think, but that's not a really big vow.

00:38:48.560 --> 00:38:52.340
But it's the small things that make the buddha paradise.

00:38:52.340 --> 00:38:56.260
It's the small things that bodhisattvas do,

00:38:56.720 --> 00:38:58.720
that are nice to other people.

00:38:59.620 --> 00:39:02.400
Of course, everybody in the world is gonna ...

00:39:03.599 --> 00:39:07.679
... stop a nuclear war or something if they can. I mean, that's obvious.

00:39:08.640 --> 00:39:10.800
But are you a good enough person 

00:39:11.839 --> 00:39:14.399
that you don't even want people to smell your breath

00:39:15.360 --> 00:39:16.980
If it might hurt them?

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:18.640
If you're very sensitive

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:22.160
about tiny things that might hurt other people

00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:25.839
then we can say you're keeping your morality. 

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:32.240
And then it's the small details that put the finishing touches

00:39:32.880 --> 00:39:36.160
on your buddha paradise, which you see in the next picture.

00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:44.640
This person decorating a Christmas tree ...

00:39:46.340 --> 00:39:50.880
If you have ever done a Christmas tree, but those of us who grew up in christian tradition

00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:53.680
our parents had us do Christmas trees.

00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:56.800
There's something cool about

00:39:57.440 --> 00:40:00.360
putting on the last ornament.

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:05.440
Everybody's looking at the tree and they say, 'is it done' and they say, 'yeah, it's done'.

00:40:06.400 --> 00:40:10.079
He said, 'wait, there's one more we should put right there'.

00:40:10.720 --> 00:40:13.359
This Christmas tree ornament

00:40:14.560 --> 00:40:20.520
is the brushing your teeth. It's the small final details

00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:27.280
that you put on your buddhahood. It's the small things that make Buddhas. 

00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:30.640
It's not the grand things. It's not the big things. It's attention

00:40:31.599 --> 00:40:33.599
to the small details

00:40:33.680 --> 00:40:38.800
of making other people happy that creates a buddha. 

00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:42.160
Next one.

00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:47.540
See if you remember this one. I'll give you a clue - yamantaka, yamantaka.

00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:58.480
This is a famous lamrim story.

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:04.719
Monks and nuns are supposed to go twice a month to sojong and confess

00:41:05.440 --> 00:41:07.440
the mistakes we made, to each other

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:10.000
and openly.

00:41:11.599 --> 00:41:13.599
The teacher said,

00:41:13.839 --> 00:41:16.959
...they struck the ?gunty. They struck the ?gunty

00:41:17.839 --> 00:41:21.199
which is a special piece of wood, it looks like a 2x4

00:41:21.840 --> 00:41:26.200
and you hit it with a another stick and it goes thunk, thunk, thunk...

00:41:26.640 --> 00:41:32.000
and that's an ancient bell before before metal was common.

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:36.740
They will hit the plank, and when you hear that 

00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:39.980
you have to go to sojong. They still do it.

00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:42.720
I made a ? with my teacher. He wanted one

00:41:43.840 --> 00:41:46.140
and we made it to the right dimensions.

00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:48.180
There's all these rules about it.

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:50.420
When you hear the ?

00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:52.880
you're supposed to .... you hold it here..

00:41:53.200 --> 00:41:55.980
you hold the ? here and you hit it like this.

00:41:56.560 --> 00:41:59.780
Then all the monks and nuns are supposed to come for confession.

00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:04.319
This teacher said, 'hey, they struck the ?gunty. Let's go.'

00:42:05.119 --> 00:42:07.838
The students said, 'no i'm not going to confess today.'

00:42:08.640 --> 00:42:10.640
The teacher said, 'what?'

00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:15.839
That's one of the main commitments of a monk, to go to sojong.

00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:19.199
The teacher said, 'what are you talking about?' He says, 'I don't have to go today.'

00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:22.740
The teacher said, 'what do you mean you don't have to go today?'

00:42:22.800 --> 00:42:26.440
He says, 'did you forget, you gave me a yamantaka initiation yesterday?

00:42:26.960 --> 00:42:31.600
I am yamantaka, I'm a buddha. I don't need to go to sojong anymore.'

00:42:32.480 --> 00:42:36.640
The teacher grabs him by the ear, he says, 'What the hell, you're yamantika?

00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:41.900
Yamantika is going to sojong with me right now.'

00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:46.660
What it means is, don't give me this stuff that you're a great tantrika,

00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:50.229
and you're beyond morality and

00:42:50.229 --> 00:42:52.760
now you have higher vision - 

00:42:53.360 --> 00:42:56.480
that's a completely mistaken idea! 

00:42:57.440 --> 00:43:00.720
If you got a secret initiation

00:43:01.200 --> 00:43:04.180
then you should be going to sojong every morning or something. 

00:43:04.380 --> 00:43:07.000
You should go more than other people.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:09.320
Because that's what gives you ...

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:13.440
gives power to your tantric practice. It's being nice to other people

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:15.280
and confessing when you make a mistake.

00:43:16.079 --> 00:43:18.079
Next.

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:27.760
This is a sad image. We always think of morality as being the roots

00:43:27.760 --> 00:43:30.800
of our practice,  the foundation of our practice.

00:43:31.800 --> 00:43:34.480
Pabongka Rinpoche, kind of flipped it around.

00:43:35.680 --> 00:43:37.335
This is a perfect picture.

00:43:37.340 --> 00:43:40.880
He said, imagine an apple tree

00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:44.640
that someone sliced it in half. Actually, he used a palm tree.

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:50.980
Somebody sliced it and they cut the top off the tree.

00:43:51.280 --> 00:43:53.760
So you're not going to get leaves, 

00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:56.720
even a single leaf is not going to come out.

00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:58.980
Therefore, you are not going to get flowers.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:03.599
Therefore, you're not going to get the fruits which always come from the flowers.

00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:06.420
You're not going to get anything. 

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:12.160
A person who is not nice to other people day to day, hour to hour, 

00:44:13.360 --> 00:44:17.400
they chop off any chance 

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:22.140
of getting those beautiful fruits of practice.

00:44:22.240 --> 00:44:23.840
Next one.

00:44:30.640 --> 00:44:33.440
This was an idea of something that my teacher asked me...

00:44:35.339 --> 00:44:41.039
Sorry, that I asked my teacher and I don't know if you remember but I asked him.

00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:47.860
The first of the five paths, the path of accumulation,

00:44:49.340 --> 00:44:54.060
you reach it when you have a personal tragedy, 

00:44:54.380 --> 00:44:57.600
but if you're on the bodhisattva track,

00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:00.136
you reach it when you get bodhichitta.

00:45:00.136 --> 00:45:04.239
I said, I don't understand what's tragic about bodhichitta?

00:45:05.680 --> 00:45:07.680
And he said, 'no no, no.

00:45:07.920 --> 00:45:11.060
It's still a theme of tragedy.

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:17.840
It's just the tragedy of every being alive, every being in this whole universe

00:45:18.800 --> 00:45:20.800
is having the same tragedy.'

00:45:22.060 --> 00:45:28.520
That communal tragedy is the beginning of  the five paths.

00:45:28.660 --> 00:45:30.840
Thinking about that tragedy

00:45:31.120 --> 00:45:34.200
is the beginning of the five paths for a bodhisattva.

00:45:34.200 --> 00:45:35.780
So really, it's the same.

00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:40.320
The puppy's having a hard time, but now all the puppies in the basket are having a hard time.

00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:44.560
We're all in this together.

00:45:44.720 --> 00:45:47.360
And that's the beginning of bodhichitta.

00:45:48.660 --> 00:45:52.140
Next picture.

00:45:52.143 --> 00:45:56.860
This is a guy shaking hands with somebody in their office.

00:45:57.440 --> 00:46:03.840
I imagine the lady is introducing them. This is Joe, he works in the advertising department 

00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:07.360
and this is Sam, he works in the computer department.

00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:10.000
They shake hands.

00:46:10.720 --> 00:46:12.720
Do you remember what this is?

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:23.119
It was a very, very cute exercise where we were supposed to close our eyes

00:46:23.920 --> 00:46:26.639
and think of the person who irritates us the most.

00:46:27.440 --> 00:46:31.780
And see if we could get ourselves upset. The problem with this kind of exercise

00:46:32.319 --> 00:46:34.899
is after about 10 minutes you forget it's an exercise.

00:46:35.760 --> 00:46:37.760
You really do get upset!

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:40.640
Let me see if I can get myself upset.

00:46:41.200 --> 00:46:42.660
How are you going to do it?

00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:45.440
I am going to think about this guy who gave me a hard time this week. 'Okay, go ahead'.

00:46:47.040 --> 00:46:50.940
Then slowly the person starts shaking. You say, 'What's going on?"

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:54.720
I got upset. The experiment worked.

00:46:55.340 --> 00:46:58.960
If it's your lama, they'll say, 

00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:03.680
'check out how it feels when you first start thinking about this person.'

00:47:04.560 --> 00:47:07.199
How does it feel? What comes up in your heart?

00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:11.560
I don't know about you, but I get this little glitch in my heart.

00:47:11.740 --> 00:47:16.500
I start to feel some kind of discomfort here or here.

00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:21.600
When I think about a person who's been bothering me or a problem that's been bothering me,

00:47:22.240 --> 00:47:26.100
I can purposely generate tension

00:47:26.320 --> 00:47:28.320
inside of myself.

00:47:28.800 --> 00:47:35.460
He says, 'let's do an exercise - try to trigger some tension in your heart,

00:47:35.920 --> 00:47:40.720
then look at that tension and get to know it, as if you are shaking hands with somebody.

00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:45.180
Get to know what it feels like

00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:48.560
when a mental affliction, negative emotion

00:47:49.520 --> 00:47:52.879
Is first coming up in your heart and keep practicing it.

00:47:53.839 --> 00:47:56.710
As soon as you feel better, and you forgot about this person,

00:47:56.710 --> 00:47:57.839
then think of them again. 

00:47:58.800 --> 00:48:00.109
See if you can get upset again.

00:48:00.109 --> 00:48:01.999
See if you can start to get upset again.

00:48:02.559 --> 00:48:07.380
Try to get familiar with what it feels like; shake hands 'Hi. This is Geshe Michael'.

00:48:07.380 --> 00:48:08.959
Hi. What's what's your name?

00:48:09.599 --> 00:48:12.576
'I am starting to get upset about this person'.

00:48:12.576 --> 00:48:15.679
'Nice to meet you. Now I know what you look like.

00:48:16.240 --> 00:48:19.839
Now I can look out for you. I can avoid you in the future'. 

00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:22.400
Next one.

00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:29.440
It's called visiting the middle of the sun. 

00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:36.479
The theme of this lamrim, which was Love the Time of the Virus.

00:48:39.599 --> 00:48:42.959
The virus is a big thing, it's spread across this whole world.

00:48:43.680 --> 00:48:46.960
I have lived a long life and I thought I saw everything.

00:48:47.760 --> 00:48:53.500
I entered my 60s and thought now nothing new is going to happen.

00:48:53.780 --> 00:48:56.000
I'm pretty set for anything that would happen.

00:48:56.940 --> 00:49:04.559
I've seen everything and nothing can upset me too much. Then this virus shows up and threatens everybody in the world.

00:49:05.200 --> 00:49:09.760
Wow, that's a big thing, that covers the whole planet.

00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:15.700
I don't know if it happened to you, but it happened to me.

00:49:15.920 --> 00:49:21.100
It's probably bad deed number nine, which is ill will;

00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:24.240
being happy when someone else has a problem.

00:49:24.246 --> 00:49:29.640
When I heard that famous, irritating, people were getting sick.

00:49:30.780 --> 00:49:35.760
I didn't want them to die or anything, but... 

00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:40.920
... i told you it was bad to be bad.

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:44.560
And then I caught myself thinking like that. 

00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:47.800
It feels like a big thing. 

00:49:48.100 --> 00:49:54.800
It feels like this problem has spread all over this planet.

00:49:55.600 --> 00:50:00.540
It feels like it is something that is difficult for me to cope with.

00:50:01.120 --> 00:50:03.120
We have just entered,

00:50:03.200 --> 00:50:05.359
after 10 years of lamrim study,

00:50:06.720 --> 00:50:11.379
we have just entered the path for people of greater capacity.

00:50:12.400 --> 00:50:15.359
We're going to open that study

00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:19.839
with the idea of bodhichitta. What is bodhichina?

00:50:19.920 --> 00:50:25.700
It's not enlightenment mind. Forget that lousy translation, incredibly bad translation.

00:50:26.500 --> 00:50:33.120
It's the wish that I could become a buddha to help countless living beings. 

00:50:34.319 --> 00:50:36.479
There is a direct experience of it

00:50:37.119 --> 00:50:40.180
in the same way that there's a direct experience of emptiness.

00:50:40.180 --> 00:50:45.440
There are parallel experiences that

00:50:45.680 --> 00:50:51.600
we must get to in this lifetime and again, you should be in meditation. 

00:50:52.560 --> 00:50:59.420
We describe an extraordinary.... what do you call it....breakthrough..

00:51:01.020 --> 00:51:04.560
A threshold experience 

00:51:05.760 --> 00:51:10.300
where you go into a deep state of meditation.

00:51:10.500 --> 00:51:14.100
Because time and space are coming from seeds,

00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:16.320
if you can mess with these seeds,

00:51:16.720 --> 00:51:19.280
then you can compact time and space.

00:51:20.079 --> 00:51:23.759
In a meditation that's not longer than a half hour.

00:51:25.119 --> 00:51:27.119
You could actually visit

00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:29.359
each person in the universe

00:51:30.300 --> 00:51:33.039
including animals and bugs and birds and fish.

00:51:33.760 --> 00:51:38.000
You could communicate with each one individually,

00:51:38.720 --> 00:51:40.720
within a half an hour.

00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:43.459
To each one you could make a commitment.

00:51:44.160 --> 00:51:48.820
You meet them, you see each one is suffering, 

00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:54.400
each one is having a difficult life and worried about the future. 

00:51:55.020 --> 00:51:56.960
You could go to each one separately and say,

00:51:57.600 --> 00:52:00.420
"I got it covered, take it easy."

00:52:00.820 --> 00:52:03.140
I used to work when I was in the university. 

00:52:03.920 --> 00:52:07.040
I got a scholarship, but they said you have to work a few hours a week.

00:52:07.680 --> 00:52:09.680
It turned out to be 30 hours a week.

00:52:10.640 --> 00:52:13.860
I had to drive a truck.

00:52:14.960 --> 00:52:19.840
Actually, first they put me in a cafeteria and they said you're going to mop the floor in the cafeteria.

00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:23.440
I quit within 10 hours. I quit on the first day.

00:52:24.480 --> 00:52:28.319
Then they said, you can drive a truck. I said, that's fun. I'll drive a truck.

00:52:29.360 --> 00:52:32.120
I drove a truck for five years.

00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:36.160
We had a guy,

00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:41.480
a permanent university employee, named Big John.

00:52:41.940 --> 00:52:47.880
His name was Big John. He's a polish guy, seven feet tall, huge guy.

00:52:49.360 --> 00:52:51.020
Everyone was afraid when they saw him.

00:52:51.020 --> 00:52:54.620
They're afraid of him, but he was extremely sweet.

00:52:55.520 --> 00:53:01.400
He would bring donuts to work and he was from Trenton, New Jersey.

00:53:03.440 --> 00:53:08.960
He would do the nicest things for us and he would cover for us.  One day we broke a truck in half.

00:53:09.680 --> 00:53:12.399
We hit a tree with the truck and we broke it in half.

00:53:13.040 --> 00:53:18.160
He covered for us, 'oh these screws weren't very tight

00:53:18.160 --> 00:53:22.000
I don't know what happened. The truck fell apart. Don't blame these guys.

00:53:22.640 --> 00:53:24.640
Don't blame these young guys.

00:53:25.040 --> 00:53:27.040
All they did was drive it.

00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:31.599
Then he winked at us and said, "I got you covered. I got you guys covered."

00:53:32.240 --> 00:53:35.560
I always think of him when I think of bodhichitta.

00:53:36.260 --> 00:53:40.680
You're gonna meet each living being in the universe directly.

00:53:41.200 --> 00:53:45.200
And you're going to say, "Big John has you covered. I got you covered. Don't worry."

00:53:45.839 --> 00:53:47.919
Don't worry about it. I got you covered. 

00:53:48.960 --> 00:53:51.421
That's bodhichitta. You should have that experience.

00:53:51.421 --> 00:53:54.240
You should work for that experience. You have to meditate.

00:53:54.880 --> 00:53:56.594
You have to study about bodhichitta.

00:53:56.594 --> 00:53:58.880
You have to study the lamrim about bodhichitta.

00:53:59.920 --> 00:54:02.000
You have to do all those steps; 

00:54:03.099 --> 00:54:05.099
exchanging yourself and others...

00:54:05.680 --> 00:54:09.780
One day you will have that experience and you will meet every living being.

00:54:10.400 --> 00:54:13.920
You will say to them, 'I got you covered'. Don't worry. I got you covered.'

00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:18.559
Big Mike is taking care of you or Big Tim or a Big Seiji.

00:54:19.200 --> 00:54:21.200
Don't worry.

00:54:21.599 --> 00:54:24.078
Don't stress out. I'm on it!

00:54:25.040 --> 00:54:28.719
That's exactly what it feels like. It's a personal commitment.

00:54:29.920 --> 00:54:31.920
 Why are we talking about that? 

00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:36.160
You're gonna do that on countless worlds. When you do it, on the day you do it,

00:54:36.720 --> 00:54:39.119
you will do it on countless worlds.

00:54:40.640 --> 00:54:46.960
An action which is committed directly with every living creature on countless worlds,

00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:52.820
doesn't have trouble taking care of a single virus on a single world.

00:54:52.940 --> 00:54:54.060
It's nothing.

00:54:54.320 --> 00:54:56.320
A virus that endangers

00:54:57.200 --> 00:55:02.240
7 or 8 billion people is nothing compared to bodhichitta. 

00:55:03.480 --> 00:55:07.180
We said, if you spill ketchup on your shirt

00:55:07.180 --> 00:55:13.920
and you deliver that shirt to the middle of the sun that's 25 million degrees Fahrenheit,

00:55:14.320 --> 00:55:17.280
probably the ketchup stain is going to disappear.

00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:22.879
You probably don't have to worry about the ketchup stain. Work on your bodhichitta.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:27.520
You will destroy the virus, by the way, by accident.

00:55:28.319 --> 00:55:30.319
Not a big thing.

00:55:30.799 --> 00:55:32.799
Next picture.

00:55:34.160 --> 00:55:36.799
Don't mess around with other paths.

00:55:37.440 --> 00:55:40.099
Learn bodhichitta. Learn to have this experience.

00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:42.880
Don't waste your time.

00:55:43.520 --> 00:55:46.259
Don't focus on other things. Focus on bodhichitta.

00:55:47.360 --> 00:55:49.840
Then you don't have to do things twice.

00:55:50.160 --> 00:55:53.840
We talked about doing things twice. This lady's in a rush.

00:55:54.240 --> 00:55:57.040
She says, I don't have time for this bodhichitta stuff.

00:55:57.680 --> 00:56:00.399
I'm gonna go straight into tantra. 

00:56:01.200 --> 00:56:04.790
You're still going to have to come back and pick up that thing you forgot,

00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:05.760
which is bodhichitta.

00:56:05.760 --> 00:56:07.999
Work on your bodhichitta first.

00:56:09.040 --> 00:56:14.639
You don't have to drive back home and pick up the bodhichitta and come back. 

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:22.319
Then this was a radical example in the next picture.

00:56:27.520 --> 00:56:31.599
This is a hard one to remember. I'm going to give you a second to think about it.

00:56:42.400 --> 00:56:44.400
I don't know if you remember this. 

00:56:46.559 --> 00:56:48.281
This is kind of complicated.

00:56:48.281 --> 00:56:57.640
A group of 60 guys and girls were about to achieve nirvana just by seeing emptiness directly and  

00:56:57.960 --> 00:57:00.720
without bodhichitta, it's  lower nirvana.

00:57:02.240 --> 00:57:08.000
Manjushri shows up and teaches them about bodhichitta. 

00:57:08.120 --> 00:57:10.980
Maybe he taught about this experience we just talked about.

00:57:13.280 --> 00:57:17.444
They were all irritated by Manjushri. They're like, don't waste our time.

00:57:17.444 --> 00:57:20.639
We are close to nirvana. We can feel it. We can taste it.

00:57:21.440 --> 00:57:24.240
We all saw emptiness already, don't waste our time.

00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:29.660
Don't talk to us about this stuff. 

